  "root_cause": "Release 4 fixture teardown could destroy the monitor receiver before the rebound socket. libzmq monitor_event sends synchronously while holding _monitor_sync; an unconsumed close event can block its shared I/O thread. Leap ARM timed out in subsequent PUSH/PULL and POLLOUT checks.",
  "correction": "Subscribe to MONITOR_STOPPED; delete the monitored socket and drain close/stop events before destroying the receiver. on_exit protects assertion and exception paths. Three new injected-failure states verify fresh traffic on the same context. No C++ or production changes.",
